  "historical_output_text": " I still recall every inch that line, every tree and blade, the sound, and sight of a walk in an abandoned playground. A few years back in highschool my friends took a liking towards it. A playground where children never come; where only memories are made by kids long forgotten.\n\nI used this playground every morning, walking my route from high ground, down, then over to my bus. It’s a path of solitude; one where no words can be said without a thought, where I am free and I know no one can hear me or care for me at this time; the sun has been out long, and no humans have shown themselves, only a dog, a lone one and he’s always on a far side, a dog without any human, just the same as a human with no one, no human that can understand the words",
